  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 152 AM MDT Sat Aug 1 2026\n\nHot dry weather expected today. Many areas will be approaching \nrecord highs today with triple digits possible. Winds pick up \nsome this afternoon, especially across the central mountains \ninto the upper Snake Plain which may be the only relief from the\nheat. Heat advisories are in effect for much of the region that\nwill be flirting with triple digits and for those mid elevation\ncommunities such as Driggs and the Bear Lake area where mid 90s\naren't as common. A dry cold front arrives for Sunday. This \nwill roll back temps nearly 10 degrees in some places. Sunday is\nwindier, but probably still holding under wind advisory levels.\nThe HRRR smoke models shows another round of smoke moving back \ninto the area. Dry weather continues into early next week with \nhighs falling into the 80s across much of the region for Monday \nand Tuesday.",
